{
  "about": "Confluence Cloud pages read through its REST API; spaces listed, content found by CQL, one page read, the children of a page, folder, whiteboard, database or embed listed, a page's comments, replies, labels and attached files listed, and an author named from an account id.",
  "base": "https://example.atlassian.net/wiki",
  "calls": [
    {
      "about": "List the spaces the account may see, 25 at a time. Answers each space's id, key, name, type and homepageId, the page children starts from. keys narrows it to spaces by key, as an address shows it (/spaces/ENG/...). When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value is the next call's cursor.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "spaces",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 500,
          "name": "keys",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/spaces",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "keys",
            "value": "{keys}"
          },
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Read one page by its id, which is in its address (/spaces/ENG/pages/123456/Title). Answers its title, status, spaceId, parentId, version and links, and its body in Confluence storage format, in body.storage.value, which is XHTML with Confluence's own tags and macros, markup and not text.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "id",
          "status",
          "title",
          "spaceId",
          "parentId",
          "parentType",
          "version",
          "body",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "page",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 20,
          "name": "id",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/pages/{id}",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "body-format",
            "value": "storage"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "List the direct children of a page, folder, whiteboard, database or embed, 25 at a time, in the order of the tree. Answers each child's id, title, status and type (page, folder, whiteboard, database or embed). To go down a level, give the child's id, and give its type with an s as kind. A child whose type is folder takes kind=folders. kind is one of pages (the default), folders, whiteboards, databases and embeds. When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value is the next call's cursor, with the same id and kind.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 65536,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "children",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 20,
          "name": "id",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "default": "pages",
          "log": true,
          "name": "kind",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "enum",
          "values": [
            "pages",
            "folders",
            "whiteboards",
            "databases",
            "embeds"
          ]
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/{kind}/{id}/direct-children",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Find content by CQL, Confluence's query language, 25 at a time, as in type = page AND space = \"ENG\" AND title ~ \"runbook\". Answers each hit's id, type, status, title and _links.webui, which names its space. When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value, percent-decoded, is the next call's cursor.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "size",
          "limit",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "search",
      "params": [
        {
          "max": 2000,
          "name": "cql",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/rest/api/content/search",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "cql",
            "value": "{cql}"
          },
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "List the comments on a page, given by its id, 25 at a time, of one kind. kind=footer is the discussion under the page and kind=inline is the comments on a passage of its text, so a page is read with both. Only the first comment of each thread is listed here; its replies are the call replies, by the comment's id. Answers each comment's id, status, pageId, version (number, authorId, createdAt) and its body, in Confluence storage format, in body.storage.value, markup and not text. A comment may have resolutionStatus (open, reopened, resolved or dangling), and an inline comment has properties.inlineOriginalSelection, the passage it is on. When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value is the next call's cursor.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "comments",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 20,
          "name": "id",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "log": true,
          "name": "kind",
          "type": "enum",
          "values": [
            "footer",
            "inline"
          ]
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/pages/{id}/{kind}-comments",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "body-format",
            "value": "storage"
          },
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "List the replies to one comment, 25 at a time. Give the comment's id and its kind, footer or inline, as comments lists it. A kind that is not the comment's is no error and answers an empty list. Answers each reply as a comment is answered, with parentCommentId, the id of the comment it answers. A reply may have replies of its own, and its id with the same kind goes down a level. When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value is the next call's cursor.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "replies",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 20,
          "name": "id",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "log": true,
          "name": "kind",
          "type": "enum",
          "values": [
            "footer",
            "inline"
          ]
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/{kind}-comments/{id}/children",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "body-format",
            "value": "storage"
          },
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "List the labels on a page, given by its id, 25 at a time. Answers each label's id, name and prefix. When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value is the next call's cursor.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 65536,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "labels",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 20,
          "name": "id",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/pages/{id}/labels",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "List the files attached to a page, given by its id, 25 at a time. Answers the metadata of each file and not the file. That is its id, title (the file's name), mediaType, fileSize in bytes, status, createdAt, version, comment, and downloadLink and webuiLink, which are paths on the site that go after _links.base. Nothing here fetches a file. When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value is the next call's cursor.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "attachments",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 20,
          "name": "id",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/pages/{id}/attachments",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Name the author of a comment or a file, given an Atlassian account id, which is version.authorId in the answers of comments, replies and attachments. Answers that account's accountId, displayName and accountType (atlassian for an Atlassian account, app for the bot user of an app, or empty) and nothing else of it. Names one account a call, so several authors are several calls. A 404 is an id that is not there, and a 403 is an account that may not view users. The name may be limited by the user's profile visibility.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 65536,
        "select": [
          "accountId",
          "displayName",
          "accountType"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "user",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 128,
          "name": "accountId",
          "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9:._-]+$",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/rest/api/user",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "accountId",
            "value": "{accountId}"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "check": "spaces",
  "credential": {
    "env": "CONFLUENCE_AUTH",
    "header": "Authorization: Basic {credential}",
    "mint": [
      "CONFLUENCE_EMAIL",
      "CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN"
    ],
    "mint_command": [
      "confluence/mint"
    ],
    "not_secret": [
      "CONFLUENCE_EMAIL"
    ]
  },
  "name": "confluence"
}
